# Crispy Gochujang Tofu Bowls

Based on [School Night Vegan - Easy Tofu Marinades](https://schoolnightvegan.com/home/easy-tofu-marinades) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20260112215657/https://schoolnightvegan.com/home/easy-tofu-marinades/))

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Sesame Gochujang Tofu

- [ ] 2 (14-ounce) blocks [extra-firm tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" }, pressed and cut into 1-inch cubes
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [toasted sesame oil]{ ing="toasted-sesame-oil" }
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [vegetable oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil" }
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, minced
- [ ] 2-3 tablespoons [gochujang]{ ing="gochujang" } (Korean chili paste), adjust to taste
- [ ] 3 tablespoons [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" } or tamari
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [light brown sugar]{ ing="light-brown-sugar" }
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [toasted white sesame seeds]{ ing="toasted-white-sesame-seeds" }
- [ ] 2 tablespoons [water]{ ing="water" }

### Bowl Components

- [ ] 2 cups [short-grain white rice]{ ing="short-grain-white-rice" } or brown rice
- [ ] 3 cups [water]{ ing="water" } (4.5 cups for brown rice)
- [ ] 4 cups [mixed vegetables]{ ing="mixed-vegetables" } (bok choy, snap peas, carrots, edamame)
- [ ] 1 tablespoon [neutral oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" } for stir-frying
- [ ] 1 cup [kimchi]{ ing="kimchi" }
- [ ] 4 cups fresh [spinach or mixed greens]{ ing="spinach-or-mixed-greens" }
- [ ] 1 [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 4 [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 1 tablespoon [toasted sesame seeds]{ ing="toasted-sesame-seeds" } for garnish
- [ ] (Optional) 4 [fried eggs]{ ing="fried-eggs" }

## Recipe

### Marinate the Tofu

1. Press [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } for at least 30 minutes to remove excess moisture, then cut into 1-inch cubes
1. In a bowl or ziplock bag, whisk together [sesame oil]{ ing="toasted-sesame-oil" }, [vegetable oil]{ ing="vegetable-oil" }, [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [gochujang]{ ing="gochujang" }, [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }, [brown sugar]{ ing="light-brown-sugar" }, [sesame seeds]{ ing="toasted-sesame-seeds" }, and [water]{ ing="water" }
1. Add [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } cubes and toss to coat. Refrigerate for minimum 30 minutes or up to overnight

### Cook the Rice

1. Rinse [rice]{ ing="short-grain-white-rice" } under cold [water]{ ing="water" } until water runs clear
1. Combine rice and [water]{ ing="water" } in a pot. Bring to a boil, reduce heat to low, cover, and simmer 15 minutes for [white rice]{ ing="short-grain-white-rice" } or 40-45 minutes for brown rice
1. Remove from heat and let sit covered for 10 minutes, then fluff with a fork

### Crisp the Tofu

1. Heat oven to 425°F and line a baking sheet with parchment paper
1. Remove [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" } from marinade (reserve marinade) and spread on baking sheet in a single layer
1. Roast for 25-30 minutes, flipping halfway through, until edges are crispy and caramelized
1. Alternatively, air fry at 400°F for 15-18 minutes, shaking basket halfway through

### Prepare Vegetables

1. Heat [oil]{ ing="neutral-oil" } in a large skillet or wok over high heat
1. Add harder [vegetables]{ ing="mixed-vegetables" } first (carrots, snap peas) and stir-fry for 2-3 minutes
1. Add softer [vegetables]{ ing="mixed-vegetables" } (bok choy, edamame) and stir-fry another 2 minutes until tender-crisp
1. Season lightly with salt or splash of [soy sauce]{ ing="soy-sauce" }

### Assemble Bowls

1. Divide [rice]{ ing="short-grain-white-rice" } among bowls
1. Arrange crispy [tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" }, stir-fried [vegetables]{ ing="mixed-vegetables" }, [kimchi]{ ing="kimchi" }, fresh spinach, and [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" } slices in sections
1. Top with [fried egg]{ ing="fried-eggs" } if using
1. Drizzle with reserved marinade (thinned with a bit of [water]{ ing="water" } if needed)
1. Garnish with sliced [green onions]{ ing="green-onions" } and [sesame seeds]{ ing="toasted-sesame-seeds" }

## Notes

- **Meal prep advantage**: Rice, tofu, and stir-fried vegetables can be prepared in advance and stored separately for 4-5 days. Assemble bowls fresh with kimchi, greens, and cucumber
- **Gochujang substitute**: 2 tsp miso paste + 1 tsp sriracha + 1/2 tsp sugar per 1 Tbsp gochujang. Flavor will differ from fermented original
- **Gochujang heat levels**: Start with 2 tablespoons for mild heat, increase to 3-4 for spicier. Gochujang varies by brand
- **Dark soy sauce substitute**: Regular soy sauce + 1/4 tsp molasses or brown sugar per 1 Tbsp dark soy
- **Lettuce wrap variation**: Serve crispy tofu in butter lettuce leaves with rice, kimchi, and vegetables for a hands-on meal
- **For extra crispiness**: Pat tofu very dry after pressing and toss with 1-2 tablespoons cornstarch before marinating
